^#sync^ {quote}
{color:red}*Omer Malik [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1759760862790249]*{color}:
It is not likely to happen and we will soon improve the design so that it never happens, but I am currently testing a change that allows us to flexibly run "actions" (like approving documents, or creating a new driver) in our service. This means that rather than running all actions just once at the end, we can accommodate some use-cases where we pre-run some actions wherever we want before running them all again at the end.

The bookkeeping for ensuring that actions are only run once is a bit overkill for our current use-case, so in our first iteration, we will only run a couple of actions flexibly (approve actions is one of them), but won't implement any checks to see if the same payload is run twice or not. Even so, for our typical use-case, I don't expect the action to be re-run with the same payload, but there is a minute possibility that this could happen. I can go into more detail if you're curious.

A check to make sure the same payload is not run twice is going to be one of the first improvements we will make.
{quote}

