Hi [~accountid:6352ad6b76b91b62562cbb6c] 

Sorry for the late response. Here is the current state with comments, marked {color:#0747a6}blue{color}:

*Spoofing:* Risk 1 - Attacker tries to log in as another user by guessing credentials or forging tokens; attacker manipulates requests to access another user's ride or payment info.

* Controls:
** SEC-1 - Use token-related data in cookies - {color:#0747a6}token-related data is stored in redux store, this is implemented same way as in food app{color}
** SEC-2 - Reuse auth from RH (no OAuth, MFA). {color:#0747a6}Done, using JWT token auth{color}
** SEC-3 - Use 1 short-living token (1-hour), after it expires we require relogin (Identity team) - {color:#0747a6}unfortunately, the JWT Auth is configured globally this way: access_token, in Live is valid for 364 days, refresh_token valid for 15m. Investigation results can check here: {color}[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RNTL-27310|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RNTL-27310|smart-link]{color:#0747a6} {color}

*Tampering:* Risk 2 *-* User attempts to modify ride pricing or ride status via manipulated requests; attacker tampers with vehicle unlock commands.

* Controls:
** SEC-4 - Order verification is done on backend - {color:#0747a6}done{color}

*Repudiation:* Risk 3 - User claims they didn’t initiate a ride or payment; attacker tries to erase logs of fraudulent activity.

* Controls:
** SEC-5 - Logging is reused from backend - {color:#0747a6}done, using the standard order flow without modifications{color}
** SEC-6 - Application frontend does not send analytics - {color:#0747a6}application frontend do send analytics to mixpanel if user accepted the cookie consent scree{color}n

*Information Disclosure:* Risk 4 - Attacker brute-forces ride or invoice IDs to access other users’ ride details or payment info; insecure storage of PII.

* Controls:
** SEC-7 UUIDs are used for all public IDs - {color:#0747a6}using vehicle UUID, but order ID is a plain numeric ID, the same we use in the Native client app.{color}

*Denial of Service (DoS):* Risk 5 - Attacker floods the API with ride requests or login attempts, locking out users or overloading the system.

* Controls:
** SEC-8 Service reuses available backend rate-limiting mechanisms - {color:#0747a6}for Auth: no modifications, user-auth endpoints are used (User Identity team owned services). For orders: Recently introduced gateway service uses similar rate limiter config like the native app services. Also, gateway service has one public no-auth endpoint for checking the availability that uses stricter rate-limiter config - the config copied from User auth public endpoint related rate limiter. {color}
** {color:#0747a6}Additionally, a kill-switch is implemented on gateway service side that will prevent invoking the internal services when enabled. {color}


