* What is ITTaxi’s *stated reason* for requiring exclusivity? {color:#ff5630}They’re working tirelessly to grow their ‘association’ and therefore would partner with us as a ‘selling’ point to convince more taxis to join them.{color}
* What specific *benefits or guarantees* does ITTaxi claim exclusivity would bring (e.g., improved service quality, alignment with local taxi cooperatives, simplified compliance, regulatory acceptance)? {color:#ff5630}access to all their taxis (60% of all licensed taxis across Italy). This means that we will be in a position to onboard a large amount of taxi supply with minimal effort vs. freefloating taxis. Taxis who form part of IT taxi are also vetter by them and the quality is more controlled than free floating.{color}
* Is ITTaxi positioning this as a *pilot or proof-of-concept project* with Bolt, or as a *long-term strategic partnership*? {color:#ff5630} Long term as they have with Uber. They proposed a 5 year agreement. We can include a clause that if their supply drop below a treshold of taxis, the agreement can be ended earlier ( i would recommend this){color}
* From Bolt’s side, what is the *commercial objective* of the cooperation — accessing ITTaxi’s network, testing the taxi model, or securing national coverage? {color:#ff5630} Yes all of the above and also what i mentioned in point 2.{color}
* What is the *scope* of exclusivity (e.g., limited to certain cities, categories, or timeframes)? {color:#ff5630} Limited to Taxis that are part of IT Taxi’s platform, country wide.{color}
* Is the exclusivity *unilateral* (Bolt restricted) or *mutual* (ITTaxi also bound not to cooperate with competitors)? {color:#ff5630} Unilateral (bolt restricted). IT Taxi work with Uber.{color}
* Are we planning there will be *minimum commitments or targets* (rides, drivers, investment) linked to the exclusivity? {color:#ff5630} No they cannot guarantee this because drivers are still self employed. Uber in fact have Acceptance Rate blocking and performance blockings for NCC drivers, but nothing for IT Taxi.{color}
* Is correct to say that this agreement would  prevent Bolt from *partnering with other taxi cooperatives or local dispatch centers* in Italy during its term? {color:#ff5630} Yes for Taxi vehicles/drivers only though. IT Taxi have  majority of Taxi Market so we need to consider either integrating and having access to 60% of the supply, or going after individual agreements for the remaining 40%.{color}
* Does the exclusivity extend to *all taxi drivers affiliated to ITTaxi*, or only to a subset participating in the project? {color:#ff5630} It’s unilateral only for Bolt, and it’s for any taxi part of the IT Taxi platform.{color}
* Will there be *co-branding or marketing obligations* that might signal joint commercial activity? {color:#ff5630} This is not allowed legally, because Taxis are considered as part of public transport. Uber also requested it and they had to decline.{color}
* How does ITTaxi currently *operate and organize drivers* — as a cooperative, association, or company? {color:#ff5630} If im not mistaken, as an association but they are a booking platform. SO effectively we will integrate with them, send the booking data to their platform, their platform will match the driver with a rider and then send back the ride info to our platform.{color}
* How many *municipalities and drivers* are effectively covered under ITTaxi’s network? {color:#ff5630} {color}[~accountid:712020:1f106747-2ab8-4efd-83fa-220b87d9f350]{color:#ff5630} can you recall this figure? If I’m not mistaken it’s in the region of 14K licenses country wide.{color}
* Are there other platforms (e.g., Uber, FreeNow) that have *refused or accepted* similar exclusivity terms with ITTaxi or other cooperatives? {color:#ff5630} Uber work with IT Taxi, FreeNow work with the free-floating taxis.{color}

