Hi thanks for the questions: below are my replies. 




* While drivers can see the bonuses in their app, do they also see the performance thresholds in advance?
{color:#bf2600}The Fleet Owner communicates them to his drivers, but we don’t mention it to the drivers and it doesn’t appear in their app. (only the bonus amount){color}
* Is there a mechanism (even informal) for drivers to dispute non-payment or flag issues if a fleet owner doesn’t pass on a bonus?
{color:#bf2600}Currently no, although nothing stopping them from writing a ticker to CS, which would make its way to me. {color}
* Does a driver’s bonus progress affect how rides are allocated or how visible they are on the app?
{color:#bf2600}No zero effect on anything driver level or fleet level other than bonus remuneration.{color}
* Is the program continuous, or is it structured in fixed campaigns? Is there a defined end date or cap on duration or spend?
{color:#bf2600}Currently it’s agreed with the Fleet Owner as a trial, open ended but can end at any time with an unofficial 1 week notice. No spend or time constraints. {color}
* Are any performance expectations or volume targets communicated to fleet owners regarding how many drivers should hit bonus thresholds?
{color:#bf2600}No in so far as a target, but they do get 50 euros per driver on a threshold (capped at 50){color}
* Are fleet owners encouraged to actively monitor or influence driver behavior to help reach those thresholds?
{color:#bf2600}Only in so much as I share the drivers finished order so far on Fridays, so the FO can motivate those close to a threshold. I do this to help the Fleet Owner, he has access to this himself in his Fleet Owner portal.{color}
* Is there any mechanism for drivers to opt in or out of the scheme, or is participation assumed by default?
{color:#bf2600}Assumed by default, and (although I don’t have full visibility), it’s up to the Fleet Owner to communicate to the drivers, so he may omit some. I don’t know.{color}
* Is Bolt ever involved in resolving disputes between drivers and fleet owners about bonus eligibility or amounts?
{color:#bf2600}No. In the past, on other programs (very rarely) it’s come up. We tell the drivers to speak to their fleet owner, and if they deem it appropriate to file a complaint with police, but that we won’t get involved. {color}
* Do fleet owners receive KPI dashboards or performance reports from Bolt to help them track how drivers are progressing?
{color:#bf2600}On Friday: I share a list of the drivers with their rides so far. {color}
{color:#bf2600}On Monday: I share a list of who hit what target and who made what bonus with the Fleet Owner. {color}
{color:#bf2600}He has access to these in his portal, but it would take some fiddly work him to get it all. {color}

