To sum it up: we can offer both OTC and prescription medicines so long as licensed pharmacies are the seller/dispensing party and Bolt remains a marketplace only; in that setup, neither Bolt nor couriers need a pharmaceutical license.

Few points to keep in mind:

* only licensed pharmacies can be onboarded to the platform;
* only state-registered medicine can be sold, regulated retail prices must be respected;
* only in-person handover is allowed - the buyer must be present to check the pack/expiry/labeling. Leaving at the door delivery is not allowed;
* prescription medicine: no dispense without prescription - app should support uploading the prescription, pharmacy handles verification. Age gate is 14+ with ID check at delivery;
* advertisement: neutral product facts can be shown. For prescription medicine advertisement is forbidden,  for OTC it’s allowed, but very tightly restricted (no minors targeting, no giveaways, no guarantees, etc).

Please let me know if you have any further questions!

