Hi Ole. Tks for reaching out. Let me go topic by topic:

{quote}Can you briefly explain what should be in the business review, possibly an example of one from another market{quote}

BR is a meeting focused on fleet performance review. Prior to the meeting, Account Managers analyze KPIs that translate fleet performance, understand what is going well and what needs to be improved and prepare a summary of their analysis + discovery questions to have a better understanding of why the fleet perform the way it does. Then, AMs meet FOs, discuss all topics prepared (fleet performance analysis) and align on next steps. BRs are supported by the Fleet Health Score methodology, that contains the KPIs that must be reviewed. Examples from [DE|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1z7sNaBoZ8y52pxdKB9bSa9tQAqJT64VlnLr3NYVYx-4/edit?tab=t.0] and [NG|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v9uM0iOPQOJM2zr92jl73tXKKA9AHU8rhDNK5feorA4/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.tiobu3fhr2ij] of BRs summarized in meeting notes and recorded in Salesforce (CRM).

{quote}similar about health score. I see we have a baseline for 2025, i.e. studies must be done this year?{quote}

No need for you to study since 1) you guys were not enrolled in the program so you're not familiar with the tiny bits of the FHS and 2) I already did the analysis myself for every market. In general lines, we expect FHS to improve 12pp from Jan to Dec 26 for all fleets in the market and 15pp for managed fleets (by AMs). I believe there is a doc called Fleet Strategy linked in the sheet where you can see baselines and targets for all markets, including DK.

{quote}Identify and develop deal opportunities. that makes sense, I am in doubt about what type of deals, and who should benefit from these.{quote}

All types of deals that impact GMV: branding, financing, rewards, specific customized contracts to ensure fleet lock-in, city expansion, etc. We're building a pipeline in Salesforce so that we can track and manage all GMV growth opps mapped and developed by local teams.On another note: I see that you crossed two KRs related to training & enablement, part of a new initiative we're starting in 2026. If AMs will execute BRs with key fleets, improve FHS of their fleets and develop GMV growth opps, we need to make sure that AMs are prepared well for the job. That's why training & enablement is required for all markets. My request is to keep the KR "Achieve grade of 90 by training module exam".Does this clarify? Let me know in case hop on a call - I'm here to support. (edited)

