Hi Team,

Here is the draft Services Agreement with our proposed changes and comments: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/10dv7NH1XgshwWYOQVI94lD8P7C_R4_K-/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/10dv7NH1XgshwWYOQVI94lD8P7C_R4_K-/edit|smart-link] 

We have reviewed the document and made a number of adjustments aimed at better protecting Bolt’s position and clarifying key terms. In particular, *we’ve addressed:*

* Excessively broad liability exclusions, by introducing carve-outs (e.g., for gross negligence or operational failures) - clause 5;
* Uncapped charges for additional services, by requiring prior written approval for costs beyond a certain threshold - added clause 4.7. and 4.8. for this particular point;
* Ambiguities around responsibilities, particularly regarding tax obligations (clause 6), compliance with laws in leased premises (clause 3.2./b), and legacy employment liabilities (clause 3.2./d);
* Imbalanced termination rights, reducing the notice period for termination by Bolt (clause 2) and ensuring that Bolt is given proper notice and opportunity to remedy non-payment before termination (clause 10.2./a);
* Inaccurate factual statements, such as references to Bolt owning the office, which have been corrected to reflect our leasehold status;
* IP rights, which were previously one-sided, are now reciprocal and allow each party to retain ownership of what they contribute (clause 9).

These changes aim to ensure the agreement reflects our actual operations and risk appetite, and that obligations are balanced and clearly defined.

To my understanding, the KPIs and detailed performance expectations are set out in the proposal (PROP CBRE GWS 257.25.02), which is why I did not include specific clauses of that nature in the Agreement.

Please note that I have not evaluated the adequacy or reasonableness of the proposed services (e.g., cleaning scope, maintenance frequency), as that falls outside my scope as legal counsel. I am operating on the assumption that the relevant teams have reviewed and approved the operational content of the proposal, and that it accurately reflects what was agreed with CBRE.

Thank you!

